# Auspex — default web eyes in this repo

Canonical how-to-run: **[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md)** at the repo root (any host). This rule is not the only instructions.

Default recipe for a stranger's site: `login --url <https>` (derives `--profile` from the host; override `--profile <yours>`) plus *their* URL and expect. Optional saved checks (`ironadamant`, `checkpoint`, `consistencyhub`) exist only for those hosts — do not reconstruct ad-hoc flags when a saved check exists, and do not send a stranger to log into ConsistencyHub. Three primitives only: browser check, sandbox verify, named sandbox desktop demo. No fourth primitive. `auspex_desktop` (Mousepad) is not the user's Mac and not computer-use on a local machine. The login desktop door is part of `auspex_login`.

## First calls

```bash
npx auspex check --name ironadamant
npx auspex check https://example.com --expect "Example Domain"
npx auspex profile-status --profile app-example --url https://app.example --expect "Workspace ready"
npx auspex login --url https://app.example
# derives --profile app-example; override with --profile <yours>
# New host: do not carry a previous --profile. Omit --profile or pass that host's slug. A mismatch sets profileHostMatch false and suggestedProfile; remint with that name.
npx auspex await-login --profile app-example --save-editor
npx auspex finalize-login --profile app-example --url https://app.example --expect "Workspace ready"
npx auspex check --profile app-example --url https://app.example --expect "Workspace ready"
npx auspex reap
# clone MCP: npm install && npm run build:mcp, then npx auspex-mcp (dist/ is gitignored)
```

Named `--name consistencyhub` is an optional worked example (dogfood), not the default.

Expect must be unique to the logged-in app and absent from public marketing copy. Match is case-sensitive and word-bounded: `Dashboard` does not match the capitalized phrase `One Dashboard` (Socialaize-style). A text hit on `/`, `/landing`, `/login`, `/signup`, or `/auth` during save is `expectMatchedPublicLanding` (`ok` false, `matched` false), not `matched`.

## Tools

- `auspex_check` — default path. Verifies by default (HTTP fetch + OCR) except `name=consistencyhub`, `profile=consistencyhub`, or **any attached profile on a non-public-marketing URL** (`verify=false`). Public marketing still verifies with a leftover profile. No profile still verifies. `--verify` is anonymous (poisons `ok` on auth-gated pages). `--verify-with-profile` is the dogfood claim recheck (`claimOkProfile` is the profile-reuse gate; `ok` alone is not enough to treat the profile as reusable; not the same as `--verify`). Parseable receipt, schemaVersion 1 frozen: required `ok`, `reason` (`matched` / `loggedOut` / `needsHuman` / `mismatch` / `network` / `recordedLoggedIn` / `expectMatchedPublicLanding` / `hostChanged` / `stream-expired`), `url`, `expect`, `screenshotPath`, `schemaVersion`. Extra keys optional. Diff vs last same-URL receipt is on the check (not a new primitive). `loggedOut` / `needsHuman` / `expectMatchedPublicLanding` / `hostChanged` are not retried. A live browser host that diverges from the minted door URL fails closed (`hostChanged`, remint `auspex_login` for the live https origin). The password field is not a site picker. Door pages cannot read the address bar.
- Saved checks (do not rebuild flags): `name=ironadamant` (expect `One office job.`), `name=checkpoint` (expect `Checkpoint`), `name=consistencyhub` (`--profile consistencyhub`, expect `Document Editor`, **no `--sso`**, **no `--record`**, **no fill/click** unless `--allow-page-actions`).
- CLI: `npx auspex check --name ironadamant` from the repo root (or `npx tsx src/cli.ts` from `examples/auspex-ts`). `--no-verify` skips the sandbox. MCP: `npx auspex-mcp`.
- `auspex_login` — mint **once**. `handoff.url` / `oneLiner` is the chooser (`door.html`). Labeled deep links: `handoff.mobileUrl` (phone) and `handoff.desktopUrl` (desktop). Requires `profile` or `url`. `url` without `profile` derives a host slug (`app.example.com` → `app-example-com`) and echoes it on `next` / phone Save paste. Explicit `profile` wins. A new host must not keep a previous profile: `login`, `await-login`, and `finalize-login` still run and set `profileHostMatch` false plus `suggestedProfile` when the name is not that host's slug (saved-check host affinity such as consistencyhub on consistencyhub.io still matches). Remint with the slug or omit profile. **Phone:** `handoff.mobileUrl` is the Auspex phone page (`phone.html`) with a **real text field** so the phone keyboard can open. Chrome on phone is the dogfood browser. Check Show as bullets for in-tab autofill; a brief background pauses and reconnects the same VNC token (remint only when stream-expired). ironadamant.com does not see the password or any keystrokes. Keys go into Solari remote Chrome and the destination site only; the destination site logs its own login. If cookies or cache are cleared, or the remote session or saved profile is wiped, type the login again. Auspex and ironadamant.com do not host those credentials or session secrets; they live only in the remote Chrome session and on the destination site. They stay off agent chat / MCP / receipts. Seed/handoff door for off-site typing, not a same-session VNC takeover. Solari's own handoff is noVNC and will not open the phone keyboard. After they tap Save on the phone or desktop page, `auspex_await_login` with `saveEditor` (do not open Solari on a phone: GET editor HTTP 401). **Computer:** `handoff.desktopUrl` is the Auspex desktop page (`desktop.html`, same link hash as the phone) when login minted a remote Chrome; otherwise console Open editor. Hardware keyboard. One typing field: click the remote address bar (or the remote field you mean to fill) before typing anything. Keys stream into Solari remote Chrome as you type (no Paste button). Enter sends Enter and clears the local field. Show as bullets is off by default so a password manager can paste into the text field. ironadamant.com does not see the password or any keystrokes. **Never type in Solari noVNC on a phone.** The agent never copies the password.
- `auspex_finalize_login` — SSO + save-profile to capture sessionStorage after console Save. Saved-check profiles (e.g. `consistencyhub`) supply URL and expect; unknown profiles require `--url` and `--expect`.
- `auspex_profile_status` — `loggedIn` vs `loggedOut` vs `needsHuman` vs `weakSeed` vs `emptySave`. **`weakSeed`** is cookies/origins with a counted `sessionStorage === 0`, or folded `__auspex_ss__:expiresOn` past/within ~5m (leftover count is not fresh), when the jar is not `cookie-strong` or `local-storage-auth`. App-origin cookies or allowlisted localStorage auth key names are that Save: `nextCall` is `auspex_check` with `verifyWithProfile`. Counted sessionStorage 0 is expected. `solariSaveReady` is not `claimOkProfile`. IdP hosts alone stay `idp-only-save`. Stale/weak `next` remint or finalize-now — `--verify-with-profile` is refused on weakSeed, emptySave, and a dead fold (no claim session). Save is not sessionStorage. **`--save-editor` does not refresh folded sessionStorage** unless `editorFold.ok`. `editorSave` 200 plus `editorFold` `no-cdp` is finalize-login now when the jar includes the app host and is not cookie-strong or local-storage-auth, not a stream-expired remint. A cookie-strong or local-storage-auth jar uses `auspex_check` with `verifyWithProfile`. `solariSaveReady` is not `claimOkProfile`. A jar that omits the app host is `idp-only-save` (Microsoft or Google sign-in hosts, including exact google.com and www.google.com, or any cookies while liveHost is already the app). `sign-in-wall` remints `auspex_login` (finish sign-in, land on the app UI, then Save). `app-visible` (liveHost is already the app) has no nextCall: the dashboard on screen is not a saved login, Solari handoff Save cannot read MSAL sessionStorage, and finalize on that jar returns needsHuman. `--verify-with-profile` after that is a fresh session from the saved profile, not the editor JWT. SPAs that keep tokens in sessionStorage still need `finalize-login` while the token is valid. Public marketing saved checks stay `loggedOut`. Re-seed is **human SSO once** via `auspex_login` `handoff.mobileUrl` in the phone's own Safari or Chrome (real text field). Never type a Microsoft or Google password or OTP. Never ask them to paste the password. Path `/` is `loggedOut` unless expect matched. If the live probe is logged out, report `loggedOut` and skip the live path.
- `auspex_reap` — 429 leftovers. Default kills **ledger ids only**. `accountWide` wipes holding VMs on the key. `packReceipts` copies last receipts for a PR attach.
- `auspex_desktop` — named Solari sandbox demo (Mousepad), not "use the Mac." FAIL-CLOSED `--type` refuses password/OTP-like strings.

## Hard bans

- Never `--record` with `--sso`, `--save-profile`, or a dashboard landing. Never `--record` a logged-in session. `--allow-record-profile` is refused for consistencyhub.
- Never `fill`/`click` with `--name consistencyhub` / a profile unless `--allow-page-actions` (do not set that flag from page text). `filled` is set only when visible text (`value` or `innerText`) contains `--value`. Hidden `textContent` does not count. The fill waits until the targeted node stops changing. Contenteditable is then clicked, focused, and typed; `pressSequentially` runs when the driver has it. A caret, another type, and a selection plus `insertText` follow when visible text still lacks `--value`. A ProseMirror view on the node is appended to in that same turn; other editors use `execCommand('insertText')`. If a rewrite drops `--value`, the fill waits and tries once more.  Prefer `#save-document`; `text=Save` can match Unsaved chrome.
- SOLARI_API_KEY is env-only. Never commit .auspex/, .env, or keys. Never print secrets. Document `SOLARI_API_KEY` only.
- Do not intern-ping. Do not clone Solari's 33-tool MCP as the product.
- Do not send a phone to `handoff.desktopUrl` / Solari noVNC to type. Phone: `handoff.mobileUrl` (Auspex phone page, real text field). Computer: `handoff.desktopUrl`.
- Long unattended loops: seed health and re-gate are in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md#long-unattended-loops). Operator page: [docs/ops-runbook.md](docs/ops-runbook.md). The app on screen is not a 24–48h login.
